************************  Technical Stuff  *******************************
OR, what it is taking at the moment to run this sucker, as of 4 Aug 1993.
**************************************************************************
        computer:  Amiga 2000
             CPU:  68030
             RAM:  13 MEGS  (1CHIP+12FAST)
      controller:  A2091
        hardrive:  1 GIG Micropolis
        floppies:  1-internal
        CD drive:  Xetec 650i (Chinon CDS-435)
           modem:  Practical Modem 14400FXSA
              OS:  AmigaDOS 2.0

BBS.baud is currently about 200k of lightly commented ARexx code, with
maybe 350k more of ARexx macros (mostly sysop routines & reports).

             The software is BBBBS, written by Richard Lee Stockton.
             The language is ARexx, written by Bill Hawes.
 The terminal engine is BaudBandit, written by Greg Cunningham.

We suggest (but do not insist) that you use an Amiga on this board.
   
